      "body": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Chemical reactions involve the breaking and making of chemical bonds. When a bond is formed between two atoms, energy is released. The same amount of energy is absorbed when the bond is broken to form neutral atoms; we call this, bond dissociation energy which is defined as,"
          },
          {
            "type": "callout",
            "tone": "definition",
            "title": "Bond dissociation energy",
            "text": "\"The average amount of energy required to break (dissociate) one mole of a particular bond in a substance.”"
          },
